from pathlib import Path
root=Path('.')
p=root/'docs/RESULTS.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s+='''\n\n## Routed switched-capacitor signed membrane packet — 2026-10-13\n\nThe physical integration parent `gf180_sc_state_packet_compact_v12` combines the native state cell, one 5x5um MIM packet, and three quarter-size transmission gates for packet parking, sampling, and weight drive. Its bbox is 527x93.45um (0.04925mm2). Magic full DRC=0, unique LVS, GDS roundtrip DRC=0 and unique LVS. Single-source control pins are exposed directly at their child terminals; only shared state/packet/supply nets use parent routing. This cut control-to-state extracted coupling from about12.7fF in the first compact-bus parent to0.15fF. The earlier v7 parent’s long blanket buses produced170mV sample-edge disturbance and up to262mV release error, despite a clean physical check; those results identify parent-route parasitics, not packet behavior.\n\nWith center state, ideal external phases, baseline1.697545V, and packet steps94mV positive /45mV negative, extracted TT27 transient gives+8.01mV/-8.10mV after packet release. The subsequent5ms drift is+0.04mV in both cases. This is a layout-specific nominal result. The previous sparse endpoint settings do not transfer: low-state handoff is+13.875mV and events net+18.356mV/+2.862mV; high-state handoff is-11.970mV and events net+7.810mV/-6.730mV. Endpoint hold drift is at most0.191mV. Thus the center map works on this routed parent, but beta dynamics, sample/drive baseline, and signed packet amplitudes still require per-range calibration. The endpoint run uses a staggered switch/source release after an initial simultaneous-edge run reached an ngspice timestep failure; the staggered transient completes.\n\nSmaller routing experiments v12/v13 retain DRC/LVS/GDS readback but have not replaced v12 as the characterized candidate. Attempts to move the MIM near the drive switch (v14-v16) retain DRC/spacing failures and are debug-only. No full-float weight mapper, autonomous sequencer, range detector, original-checkpoint recurrence replay, PVT/noise/mismatch sweep, 25-actor service, or full-chip layout is qualified.\n\nEvidence: `artifacts/analog_asic/layout/gf180_sc_state_packet_compact_v12/qualification.json`; center run `artifacts/analog_asic/results/gf180_sc_state_packet_compact_v12_center_recalibrated_5ms_v2.json`; endpoint run `artifacts/analog_asic/results/gf180_sc_state_packet_compact_v12_endpoints_staggered_5ms_v2.json`; extracted capacitance `artifacts/analog_asic/layout/gf180_sc_state_packet_compact_v12/gf180_sc_state_packet_compact_v12_cap.spice`. Earlier failed and superseded outputs remain preserved.\n''';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=root/'docs/DECISIONS.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s+='''\n\n## Continue with routed switched-cap packet; recalibrate at each state range — 2026-10-13\n\nThe center-state packet method remains the selected next implementation because the compact parent now passes DRC/LVS/GDS readback and delivers matched signed8mV-class updates with less than0.05mV drift over5ms. Use parent v12 while calibrating; the center packet steps must not be reused at endpoints without measurement. The endpoint transient shows beta/handoff errors up to13.9mV and wrong/small updates for some old packet settings. Continue with state-conditioned beta/baseline and positive/negative packet transfer calibration, then exercise the original-float recurrence. This is a provisional article implementation, not an acceptance claim. The first long-bus parent is rejected functionally because routed control coupling dominated the update; compact reroutes remain experiments until extracted simulation passes.\n\nEvidence: `artifacts/analog_asic/layout/gf180_sc_state_packet_compact_v12/qualification.json`, center and endpoint reports cited in RESULTS.md.\n''';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=root/'docs/ARCHITECTURE.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s+='''\n\n## Routed switched-capacitor membrane packet — 2026-10-13\n\nThe active charge-delivery candidate uses one shared MIM packet per update channel: sample/park the packet against membrane state, disconnect the sample path, drive the bottom plate from an analog weight-dependent source, then release the packet while the membrane stores the resulting charge. Weight determines the signed charge amplitude; it does not change presynaptic firing frequency. The current v12 physical parent integrates the state storage, packet capacitor, and park/sample/drive TGs. It exposes one-source controls directly at their child pins and routes only shared nets across the parent. Control routing matters physically: an earlier blanket-bus parent had extracted control-to-state coupling above12fF and caused roughly170mV sample-edge disturbance.\n\nUse the nominal v12 center transfer as a calibration point only. At TT27 with externally supplied phase timing and voltage maps,94mV/45mV packet steps produce+8.01/-8.10mV and hold within0.04mV over5ms. Low/high state response, beta mapping, analog weight source, physical timing, saturation detector, full PLIF recurrence, and full-chip service remain open. Keep original float parameters; no QAT or quantized membrane path defines analog precision.\n''';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=root/'docs/PROGRESS.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s+='''\n\n2026-10-13 routed packet milestone: compact parent v12 now passes full DRC/LVS/GDS readback at0.04925mm2. Direct child-pin control exposure removes long-bus control coupling; routed center-state packet calibration gives+8.01/-8.10mV signed updates with0.04mV drift at5ms. Staggered endpoint run completes, but handoff errors reach13.9mV and prior sparse packet maps miss target at low/high states. Continue state-conditioned beta/baseline/packet calibration and original-float replay; no full-chip layout or 25-actor service pass yet. Exact pre-update docs: `artifacts/analog_asic/documentation_history/project_docs_before_routed_sc_packet_20261013T091833.zip`.\n''';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
